## 5. ALWAYS use field-level validation on forms

### ❌ Forbidden — only showing a banner, no field highlighting:
```js
if (!billNum) return showErr('bill-verify-error', 'Enter Bill Number.')
if (!actual || actual <= 0) return showErr('form-error', 'Amount required.')
```

### ✅ Required — mark the specific field red AND show banner if needed:
```js
if (!billNum) {
  cosmosFieldError(document.getElementById('bill-number-input'), 'Required')
  return
}
if (!actual || actual <= 0) {
  cosmosFieldError(document.getElementById('actual-bill'), 'Enter a valid amount')
  return
}
```

Clear field errors when the user starts fixing them:
```js
document.getElementById('bill-number-input').addEventListener('input', function() {
  cosmosFieldClear(this)
})
```

These functions are defined in `src/public/js/cosmos-ui-polish.js`:
- `cosmosFieldError(inputEl, message)` — red border + error text below field
- `cosmosFieldClear(inputEl)` — removes error state
- `cosmosFieldOk(inputEl)` — green border (for live validation)

