## 9. CSS variable usage — never hardcode colours

### ❌ Forbidden:
```js
el.style.background = '#dcfce7'
el.style.color = '#065f46'
el.style.borderColor = '#6ee7b7'
```

```css
.my-element { color: #1E40AF; background: #EFF6FF; }
```

### ✅ Required — always use the design system variables:
```css
.my-element { color: var(--acc2); background: var(--accL); }
```

Available variables (defined in `foundry-prototype.css`):
```
--acc, --acc2, --accL, --accD          ← blues
--green, --greenL                       ← greens
--red, --redL                           ← reds
--gold, --goldL                         ← ambers
--teal, --tealL                         ← teals
--orange, --orangeL                     ← oranges
--border, --card, --bg                  ← surfaces
--text1, --text2, --text3               ← text hierarchy
--navy, --navy2                         ← sidebar dark
```

