## 11. Tech stack constraints — read before writing any code

This project uses **vanilla JS and CSS only**. No React, Vue, Angular, or any frontend framework.

- All JS files are loaded with plain `<script>` tags — **no ES module syntax**
- Use `window.functionName = function() {}` for shared utilities — not `export`
- Do not `import` anything — there is no bundler
- Do not install npm packages for frontend features — only backend dependencies use npm
- Do not use GSAP, Framer Motion, Animate.css, or any animation library
- All CSS animations must be `@keyframes` in plain CSS files

All polish utility functions (`cosmosToast*`, `cosmosBtnLoading`, `cosmosSkeleton*`, etc.) are on `window` and available globally in every JS file once `cosmos-ui-polish.js` is loaded.

---

## 12. New feature checklist — before marking any UI feature as done

Before saying a UI feature is complete, verify all of the following:

- [ ] All data fetches show skeleton loaders — no blank states, no "Loading…" text
- [ ] All async buttons use `cosmosBtnLoading()` / `cosmosBtnDone()` / `cosmosBtnSuccess()`
- [ ] All API errors show `cosmosToastError()` — no `alert()` anywhere
- [ ] All form required fields use `cosmosFieldError()` on failed validation
- [ ] Clickable table rows have `.tr-link` class
- [ ] Dashboard stat numbers use `cosmosCountUp()`
- [ ] Empty states have headline, subtext, and action button where applicable
- [ ] No hardcoded hex colours — CSS variables only
- [ ] `cosmos-ui-polish.css` and `cosmos-ui-polish.js` are linked in the HTML file
